  <h2 class="mt-0">Neighbours, practically</h2>
  <p>If you're in Redhill, off the A60 heading north, or in Daybrook near Arnot Hill Park and the old brewery, Arnold is just round the corner. From Bestwood Village or Bestwood Park it's a short drive east. That makes the 7:30am drop-off and 5pm collection for daycare easy to fit around the school run or the drive to work.</p>
  <p>And because Redhill, Daybrook and much of Bestwood sit in Gedling borough, you'll be pleased to know Paws 2 Purrs is licensed by Gedling Borough Council and fully insured.</p>

  <h2>Country parks all around you</h2>
  <p>Dog owners round here are spoilt. Bestwood Country Park, with its woodland, open grassland and the Mill Lakes, is on the doorstep for Bestwood and Redhill. Burntstump Country Park is just north of Arnold off the A60. Arnot Hill Park in Daybrook is great for a gentle loop.</p>
  <p>Vanessa's pack walks are made of the same ingredients: woodland, farm fields and water spots, with ball play on the way. Most dogs are off lead or on long lines. She'll tell you exactly where your dog will be walking at your meet &amp; greet.</p>

  <h2>Finding the right fit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Out at work all day?</strong> <a href="/dog-daycare-arnold-nottingham/">Doggy daycare in Arnold</a>: a small pack, long walks and a big enclosed garden.</li>
    <li><strong>Just need the walk done?</strong> <a href="/dog-walking-arnold-nottingham/">Dog walks include pick-up and drop-off</a>, so Vanessa (or her son) collects and returns your dog.</li>
    <li><strong>Holiday, wedding or work trip?</strong> <a href="/dog-boarding-arnold-nottingham/">Home boarding</a> from one night up, in a home, not kennels.</li>
    <li><strong>Rabbits, guinea pigs or a cat?</strong> <a href="/cat-sitting-arnold-nottingham/">Cat pop-ins and small animal feeds</a> while you're away.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reliable, year after year</h2>
  <p>"Reliable" comes up again and again. Karena, whose dog Vanessa and her son walk, calls them "a lovely team &amp; very reliable". Lola the Labrador has been coming for over three years, and Gracie for more than five.</p>
